.TH KSNIP-PYQT6 1 "2026-10-26" "ksnip-pyqt6 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ksnip-pyqt6 \- screenshot and annotation tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ksnip-pyqt6
.RI [ IMAGE ]
.br
.B ksnip-pyqt6
.RB [ \-r | \-l | \-f | \-m | \-a | \-u | \-t ]
.RB [ \-d " SECONDS" ]
.RB [ \-c ]
.RB [ \-s | \-p " PATH" | \-o ]
.br
.B ksnip-pyqt6
.RB [ \-e " IMAGE" ]
.RB [ \-s | \-p " PATH" | \-o ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ksnip-pyqt6
takes screenshots of the desktop and opens them in an annotation editor.
A screenshot can cover all screens, the current screen, a rectangular area
chosen with the mouse, the last selected area, the active window or the
window under the cursor.
.PP
The editor supports freehand drawing, lines, arrows, rectangles, ellipses,
text, numbered markers, stickers, inserted images and watermarks. Items can
be moved, resized, rotated, duplicated and reordered, and the result can be
saved as PNG, JPEG, BMP or WebP, exported to SVG, copied to the clipboard,
printed or uploaded with a user supplied script.
.PP
When a file name or
.B \-e
is given on the command line, the image is opened in the editor instead of
starting a new capture. A single dash
.RB ( \- )
reads the image from standard input.
.PP
Only one instance of the program runs per user session. A second invocation
forwards its arguments to the running instance and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-rectarea
Capture a rectangular area selected with the mouse.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-lastrectarea
Capture the area used by the previous rectangular capture.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fullscreen
Capture all screens.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-current
Capture the current screen.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-active
Capture the active window.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-windowundercursor
Capture the window under the mouse cursor.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-portal
Capture through the desktop portal. This is the recommended mode on Wayland.
.TP
.BI \-d " SECONDS" ", \-\-delay " SECONDS
Wait the given number of seconds before capturing.
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cursor
Include the mouse cursor in the screenshot.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-save
Save the screenshot to the configured default directory without opening the
editor, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-p " PATH" ", \-\-saveto " PATH
Save the screenshot to
.I PATH
without opening the editor, then exit.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-upload
Upload the screenshot with the configured script without opening the editor,
then exit.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-edit
.I IMAGE
Open an existing image in the editor.
.TP
.BI \-\-language " LOCALE"
Use the given locale for the user interface instead of the system locale, for
example
.B es
or
.BR es_EC .
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ksnip/ksnip\-pyqt6.conf
User settings, written with QSettings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ksnip/ksnip\-pyqt6/
Directory holding the images imported into the sticker selector.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ksnip/ksnip\-pyqt6/
Application data, including the images used for watermarks.
.SH EXAMPLES
Capture a rectangular area and include the cursor:
.PP
.RS 4
ksnip-pyqt6 \-r \-c
.RE
.PP
Wait five seconds, then capture all screens and save the result:
.PP
.RS 4
ksnip-pyqt6 \-f \-d 5 \-s
.RE
.PP
Open an image that already exists:
.PP
.RS 4
ksnip-pyqt6 \-e screenshot.png
.RE
.PP
Save a screenshot of the active window to a specific file:
.PP
.RS 4
ksnip-pyqt6 \-a \-p /tmp/window.png
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
when the arguments are invalid or the capture or save operation fails.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR scrot (1),
.BR spectacle (1),
.BR flameshot (1)
